mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Kish Sea Watch Backend API\n\nThis canister stores the monitored beaches of Kish Island, community sea-condition reports and official warnings, and exposes them to the app frontend and to OQL data queries. It does not fetch marine or weather data itself; the frontend reads Open-Meteo directly.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\n- `listBeaches`, `getBeach`, `listReports`, `listReportsForBeach`, `listPublishedWarnings` and `getApiDoc` are open queries and work for anonymous callers.\n- `submitReport` requires a signed (non-anonymous) caller; an anonymous caller receives `#err(#notAuthorized)`.\n- `addBeach`, `updateBeach`, `listAllWarnings`, `createWarning`, `setWarningPublished` and `reviewReport` require an admin role; any other caller receives `#err(#notAuthorized)`.\n- The first caller of `_initialize_access_control` becomes the admin; later callers become regular users. A principal that never signed in through the app frontend is unregistered and is not an admin.\n- The frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin (published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available). An agent holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`); such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\n## Beaches\n\n- `listBeaches() : [Beach]` returns all beaches. `getBeach(id : Nat) : ?Beach` returns one or null.\n- `Beach = { id : Nat; nameEn : Text; nameFa : Text; latitude : Float; longitude : Float; descriptionEn : Text; descriptionFa : Text; active : Bool }`. Latitude/longitude are decimal degrees (WGS84).\n- Four beaches are seeded on first deploy: Marjan Beach, Simorgh Beach, Mir Mahna Coastal Park and Fisherman Beach Park.\n- `addBeach(...)` and `updateBeach(...)` are admin-only and return `Result<Beach>` (`#ok` or `#err`). `updateBeach` returns `#err(#notFound)` for an unknown id.\n- `ensureBeachesSeeded()` is an open update that seeds the four beaches only when the store is empty; it is idempotent and safe to call repeatedly.\n\n## Community reports\n\n- `listReports() : [Report]` and `listReportsForBeach(beachId : Nat) : [Report]` are open queries.\n- `submitReport(beachId : Nat, kind : ReportKind, note : Text) : Result<Report>` requires a signed caller. New reports start with `status = #unverified` and `reviewedAt = null`; they are unverified until an admin reviews them.\n- `Report = { id : Nat; beachId : Nat; kind : ReportKind; note : Text; submittedAt : Int; status : ReviewStatus; reviewedAt : ?Int }`. `submittedAt` and `reviewedAt` are nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (signed Int).\n- `ReportKind` is one of `#roughWater`, `#calmWater`, `#strongCurrents`, `#waterClarity`, `#jellyfish`, `#unusualWaves`, `#otherHazard`. `ReviewStatus` is `#unverified`, `#verified` or `#dismissed`.\n- `reviewReport(id : Nat, status : ReviewStatus) : Result<Report>` is admin-only and sets `reviewedAt` to the current time; unknown ids return `#err(#notFound)`.\n\n## Official warnings\n\n- `listPublishedWarnings() : [Warning]` is an open query returning only published warnings.\n- `listAllWarnings() : Result<[Warning]>` is admin-only and returns every warning including unpublished drafts.\n- `createWarning(beachId : ?Nat, messageEn : Text, messageFa : Text, severity : WarningSeverity, published : Bool) : Result<Warning>` is admin-only; `issuedAt` is set to the current time. `beachId = null` means island-wide.\n- `setWarningPublished(id : Nat, published : Bool) : Result<Warning>` is admin-only; unknown ids return `#err(#notFound)`.\n- `Warning = { id : Nat; beachId : ?Nat; messageEn : Text; messageFa : Text; severity : WarningSeverity; issuedAt : Int; published : Bool }`. `issuedAt` is nanoseconds since the Unix epoch. `WarningSeverity` is `#info`, `#advisory`, `#warning` or `#danger`.\n\n## Errors and retry safety\n\n- Mutating endpoints return `Result<T>` with `#err(#notAuthorized)`, `#err(#notFound)` or `#err(#invalidInput : Text)`; they do not trap on caller errors.\n- `submitReport`, `createWarning` and `addBeach` are not idempotent: each successful call creates a new record with a fresh id, so a retried call after an ambiguous failure can create a duplicate. Re-read the list before retrying.\n- `updateBeach`, `reviewReport`, `setWarningPublished` and `ensureBeachesSeeded` are idempotent for the same arguments.\n\n## Data queries (OQL)\n\n- `schema()` and `execute(queryJson)` expose the stored data. `beach` and `warning` are public; `report` is controller-only. Timestamps are nanoseconds; report `kind`/`status` and warning `severity` are exposed as tag text.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- Weather and marine measurements are not stored here; the app shows them from Open-Meteo with their own timestamps and marks forecasts as estimates.\n- A beach being listed or a warning being absent does not mean the water is officially safe; never present forecast-derived conditions as an official safety guarantee.";
  };
};
